 "description": "Correlation (weekly returns), annualized covariance, beta vs S&P 500, volatility, max drawdown, calendar-year returns, fund facts (fees, yield, AUM) or stock fundamentals (market cap, P/E), and ETF holdings overlap with top common positions, for a pair of US stocks or ETFs. Popular pairs come from PairBook's precomputed matrix; any other pair of covered symbols is computed on demand from the weekly return series. Example: a=QQQ, b=VOO. Symbol order does not matter. Covers ~4,700 US-listed stocks and ETFs only (no crypto, no foreign listings, no inverse/leveraged short funds, no intraday data); figures use weekly closes and refresh once per trading day. Unknown tickers return an error: resolve them with resolve_symbol first.",
